# Technical Reference — Wedding Web App

This document describes the app as it exists in this repository today. It is written for developers and other technical readers. It does not describe planned work. For the roadmap, see `WEDDING_PLAN.md`.

Wedding-day operations features are documented in `docs/ADMIN_OPS.md`: duties, salami audit (`admin.auditGift`), phones-down freeze (`freeze.*`, `admin.freeze`), emergency blast (`admin.blastList`), Door swipe and `admin.setTable`, and group themes and presets.

---

## 1. Architecture overview

| Layer | Technology | Location |
|---|---|---|
| Front end | Static HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript (no build step, no framework) | repo root, `css/`, `js/`, `admin/` |
| Offline / install | Service worker + Web App Manifest (PWA) | `sw.js`, `manifest.json`, `icons/` |
| Backend API | Google Apps Script web app (one file) | `apps-script/Code.gs` |
| Database | One Google Spreadsheet (one tab per entity) | created by `setup()` |
| File storage | Google Drive folder `Wedding/` | created by `setup()` |
| Local mock backend | In-browser fake API | `demo-data/demo-api.js` |
| Hosting | Any static host (README targets GitHub Pages) | — |

Request flow:

```
Browser page → js/api.js (API.call) ──POST text/plain JSON──► Apps Script doPost(e)
					 │                                             │
					 └── demo mode: window.DEMO_API.handle()       ├─ PUBLIC_ACTIONS / ADMIN_ACTIONS
																   └─ SpreadsheetApp / DriveApp / CacheService
```

